Local review patch: retain T6032 failure propagation across cached startup
Base: reviewed m1n1 2460b604c6f016956ead711823605eea840c602e, after adapted 0006
Provenance: AI-assisted Debian project work; not submitted upstream.

Reject uninitialized or failed T6032 startup, stop payload/HV continuation,
and report S_BADSTATE to proxy callers. Preserve other SoCs' best-effort
continuation. Static stacks remove allocation branches, not failure status.
Initialization preflight already returns -1; it must complete before release.
Existing cpufreq, PCIe, display and USB preludes are not reordered/rolled back.
This is not a global proxy sandbox or native boot approval.

